# Per-plan isolated workspaces for superpowers:subagent-driven-development
.worktrees/

# Film frames — hundreds of PNGs, regenerated by Noir.Editor.Film.Render.
# The encoded morning.webp is kept; the frames it was made from are not.
docs/film/*.png

# Bought art. 1.4GB imported, licensed per seat, and re-importable from the Asset Store,
# so it is a working-copy asset rather than a repository one. Remove this deliberately if
# it should be vendored (see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-poly-universal-pack-integration-design.md).
Assets/polyperfect/
Assets/polyperfect.meta

# llama.cpp's native binaries, which LLMUnity downloads on demand: every backend for every
# platform, ~4GB, of which this machine runs exactly one. LLMUnity fetches them again from
# LlamaLib when they are missing, so they are a working-copy asset like the art above.
Assets/StreamingAssets/
Assets/StreamingAssets.meta

# The PlayMode test runner writes a throwaway bootstrap scene into Assets/ and does
# not always clean it up. It is per-run (the GUID changes) so it is never worth keeping.
Assets/InitTestScene*.unity
Assets/InitTestScene*.unity.meta

# A report about a Unity account. Redacted, but not something to commit.
ai-probe.txt

# ---- REAL NAMES STAY ON THIS MACHINE ----
#
# The owner reversed the old NO OWNER NAMES rule on 2026-08-04 so that real 1991
# residents can be researched for design - who lived where, how households sat on
# the street. See the header of Content/parcel-county.txt for the full wording.
#
# Two of his three conditions are about where a name may GO: nothing ships with a
# real name, and no real name leaves this machine. THIS REPO PUSHES TO
# github.com/mgagnon57/SerialKillerGame, which is exactly the kind of leaving he
# meant - a public remote, and git never forgets. So the rule gets a mechanism
# instead of a memory: anything holding a real name lives in one of these and is
# ignored here, so forgetting is not enough to publish it.
Content/private/
docs/research/private/
*.private.txt
*.private.md

# THE AUTHORED NOTES ARE LOCAL. Content/parcel-notes.txt is written by the game's own
# parcel editor and now carries NAMES - who lived on a lot, what traded there. This repo
# pushes to a public GitHub remote, so a tracked notes file means every name typed into
# the editor is published on the next push. Untracked 2026-08-04 for that reason; see the
# header of Content/parcel-county.txt for the rule it belongs to. Keep your own backup -
# it is the only copy of everything you have authored.
Content/parcel-notes.txt
Content/parcel-notes.txt.bak
Content/parcel-notes.txt.tmp

# Generated by tools/md2html.py from the markdown beside them. Derived, so not tracked -
# regenerate rather than commit, or they go stale the first time a doc is edited.
docs/*.html

# Superpowers skill scratch - ledgers, briefs and review packages for in-flight plans.
# Working state, not history; the plans and specs under docs/superpowers/ are the record.
.superpowers/

# Written by the game every time it builds - what it did with each of the owner's rulings.
# Derived, rewritten on every run, and meaningless without the run that produced it.
tools/game-verdict.json

tools/.verified/

tools/__pycache__/

# ---- AI REFERENCE ART: A WORKING-COPY ASSET, AND A LOUD ONE ----
#
# 24 MB of AI impressions of Rossville in 1991, generated 2026-08-06, sitting inside Assets/
# where Unity imports them. Their own README is unambiguous about what they are:
#
#     "Mood, not measurement ... Do not measure anything off these. Do not cite them.
#      Do not let them settle a question."
#
# Against docs/SOURCES-OF-TRUTH.md they sit BELOW authored: parcel-1991.txt is authored by
# somebody who was there and outranks the sources; these are authored by a model that has
# never been there and outrank nothing. They are a target to build toward and to argue with,
# which is worth keeping on disk and is not worth 24 MB of repository.
#
# Same treatment as the pack and the llama binaries above: kept in the working copy, not
# vendored. If they should ship, remove this deliberately.
#
# MOVED OUT OF Assets/ ON 2026-08-09, which is the other half of the same argument. Inside
# Assets/ Unity imported every one as a Sprite asset with mipmaps - build time, Library space and
# a GUID apiece - for pictures whose own README forbids them settling anything. They live in
# docs/reference/Rossville1991/ now, beside the prompts that made them, where they can be opened
# and argued with and cannot end up in a build.
#
# THE PATTERN MUST STAY SPECIFIC. `docs/**/*.png` would untrack docs/snapshots, which is 129
# committed frames and a deliberate regression baseline.
docs/reference/**/*.png

# ---- THE UNITY AI GENERATORS OUTPUT CACHE ----
#
# com.unity.ai.assistant writes it, Unity reads it, and NOTHING in this project names it - a
# search for the literal string over the whole tree with ignores disabled returns zero hits.
# 24 MB in 24 files across twelve GUID-named folders, and 99.9% of those bytes are a SECOND COPY
# of the twelve PNGs in Assets/Noir/Reference/Rossville1991/ - confirmed file by file. The unique
# content is 23 KB of sidecar JSON carrying the prompts, the model and customSeed -1, which is
# kept beside the pictures as Reference/Rossville1991/prompts/.
#
# Ignored rather than merely untracked because a generation run recreates it, and until now the
# only thing between it and a public remote was the rule in CLAUDE.md saying never `git add -A`.
# The pack, the llama binaries and the reference art each got a mechanism; this had a rule.
#
# TRAP FOR ANYONE RE-CHECKING: `git check-ignore -v` on a directory WITH a trailing slash returns
# rc=0 citing a BLANK line and echoes the queried path back as though it were the pattern. It does
# that for every untracked directory in this tree. Query a real FILE path.
GeneratedAssets/

# ---- PLAYWRIGHT MCP SESSION LOGS ----
#
# The browser tool writes per-session console logs and page snapshots here whenever an agent
# drives a browser (first appeared 2026-08-16, the streetview reference session). Transient
# debugging artifacts, regenerated every session, never read back.
.playwright-mcp/
/nightly/
